ABSTRACT

The AI Smart Waste Segregation Robot is an Arduino-based educational prototype that demonstrates automatic waste sorting using sensors and servo motors. It helps explain how automation can improve waste management and environmental awareness.

---

MATERIALS USED

- Arduino Uno R3
- HC-SR04 Ultrasonic Sensor
- 3 × SG90 Servo Motors
- OLED Display
- Active Buzzer
- Red, Yellow and Green LEDs
- Breadboard
- Jumper Wires
- 220Ω Resistors
- 5V Power Supply
- Three Waste Bins
- Robot Base

---

CIRCUIT CONNECTIONS

- Ultrasonic TRIG → D2
- Ultrasonic ECHO → D3
- Servo 1 → D5
- Servo 2 → D6
- Servo 3 → D7
- Buzzer → D8
- Green LED → D9
- Yellow LED → D10
- Red LED → D11
- OLED SDA → A4
- OLED SCL → A5
- VCC → 5V
- GND → GND

---

WORKING PRINCIPLE

The ultrasonic sensor detects an object placed near the robot. The Arduino processes the sensor data and activates the programmed servo motor to demonstrate sorting. The OLED display shows the system status, LEDs indicate operation, and the buzzer provides an audible notification. After completing the sorting cycle, the robot returns to standby mode.

---

RESULT

The prototype successfully demonstrated automatic object detection, servo motor operation, and status indication using the Arduino platform.

